{%- comment -%}
  AJ Pop-up Shops — a paper pop-up book whose pop-up is a shop.

  WHAT IT IS FOR. The store's focused shops — skate, pickleball, whatever runs
  next — need somewhere on the homepage that is not another grid of collection
  tiles. A tile row says "here are some categories". A pop-up book says these
  are temporary and there is a new one, which is the same promise the rest of
  the store already makes: a Yoink for a day, a tee for a week, a bin for a
  week. The mechanic IS the message, so it is worth the pixels.

  THE WORD MATTERS AND IT IS A COMMITMENT. "Pop-up" tells a customer this shop
  will not be here forever. If these become permanent categories the section is
  lying in a small way, and the brand's whole register is not doing that — so
  either they rotate, or this gets renamed. See the theme note in the schema.

  THE LINKS ARE THE CONTENT; THE BOOK IS DECORATION. Every shop renders as an
  anchor in the markup before any script runs. No JavaScript, a failed asset
  load, or a crawler all get a plain readable list of shops. `aj-popup-shops.js`
  swaps that for the book only once it is actually running. This is deliberate
  and it is the same reason `aj-cadence` renders real dates server-side before
  correcting them in the browser.

  NOT ADDED TO templates/index.json. The theme editor holds authority over the
  settings of sections that have been touched there, and a repo-side edit to
  that file has been observed not taking on the live theme while CSS from the
  same commit went live immediately. Add this from the theme editor — Add
  section, "Pop-up shops" — and it will carry its own settings from there.

  ART PER SHOP, NOT ONE MASCOT. Each block takes its own image, because that is
  the entire argument for a pop-up book over a sandwich: what rises off the page
  can be a half-pipe for one shop and a court for the next, so the drawing does
  the wayfinding instead of a label under an identical icon. With no image the
  block falls back to the shop's name set in the brand face, which is a
  legitimate look, not a broken one.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'aj-popup-shops.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'aj-popup-shops.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign shops = section.blocks
-%}

{%- if shops.size > 0 -%}
  <section
    class="aj-popup"
    data-aj-popup
    data-interval="{{ s.interval }}"
    data-auto="{{ s.auto }}"
    style="background: {{ s.background }};"
    aria-label="{{ s.title | default: 'Pop-up shops' | escape }}"
  >
    <div class="aj-popup__inner">
      {%- if s.title != blank or s.subtitle != blank -%}
        <header class="aj-popup__head">
          {%- if s.title != blank -%}
            <h2 class="aj-popup__title" style="font-size: {{ s.title_size }}px;">{{ s.title }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if s.subtitle != blank -%}
            <p class="aj-popup__sub">{{ s.subtitle }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </header>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        The book. Aria-hidden because everything inside it is duplicated in the
        plain list below — a screen reader should hear each shop once, and the
        list is the version that reads correctly.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="aj-popup__spread">
        <div class="aj-popup__scene" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="aj-popup__book">
        {%- comment -%}
          ORDER IS THE LAYERING, and it is the order a pop-up book is actually
          assembled in: the paper, then the braces glued to it, then the piece
          they hold up. Painting the page last put it in front of the card's
          feet and swallowed the braces entirely.
        {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="aj-popup__board"></div>
          <div class="aj-popup__stack"></div>
          <div class="aj-popup__page aj-popup__page--l"></div>
          <div class="aj-popup__page aj-popup__page--r"></div>
          <div class="aj-popup__gutter"></div>
        <div class="aj-popup__struts" data-aj-struts>
          <div class="aj-popup__strut aj-popup__strut--left"></div>
          <div class="aj-popup__strut aj-popup__strut--right"></div>
        </div>
        <ul class="aj-popup__stage">
          {%- for block in shops -%}
            {%- assign b = block.settings -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              ONE SHOP AS AN ARRANGEMENT, NOT A CARD. Six scenery cut-outs in an
              arc, the shop's own artwork standing in front of them, and a paper
              tag on the platform. The scenery is deliberately generic paper
              shapes in the shop's colour — it is the SET, and the artwork is
              what identifies the shop. Positions are inline custom properties
              because they are composition, not style: moving a tree is a
              decision about this shop, and belongs beside it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <li class="aj-popup__pop" data-aj-pop {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <div class="aj-popup__vfold"></div>

              {%- if b.scenery != blank -%}
                <span class="aj-popup__set">
                  {{ b.scenery | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag: alt: '', widths: '450, 700, 900', loading: 'lazy' }}
                </span>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if b.scenery_mid != blank -%}
                <span class="aj-popup__set aj-popup__set--mid">
                  {{ b.scenery_mid | image_url: width: 700 | image_tag: alt: '', widths: '350, 520, 700', loading: 'lazy' }}
                </span>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if b.image != blank -%}
                <span class="aj-popup__sign">
                  {{
                    b.image
                    | image_url: width: 520
                    | image_tag:
                      class: 'aj-popup__art',
                      alt: b.name,
                      widths: '260, 380, 520',
                      loading: 'lazy'
                  }}
                </span>
              {%- endif -%}

              <a class="aj-popup__label" href="{{ b.link | default: '#' }}" tabindex="-1">{{ b.name }}</a>
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
        <div class="aj-popup__cast" data-aj-cast></div>

          <div class="aj-popup__leaf" data-aj-leaf></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        THE PAGE CONTROLS, AND THEY ARE OUTSIDE THE BOOK ON PURPOSE.

        The book is aria-hidden — every card in it is a duplicate of the list at
        the bottom, and a screen reader should hear each shop once. Focusable
        buttons inside an aria-hidden subtree is a genuine accessibility fault
        (you can tab to a control the assistive tree says is not there), so they
        sit alongside it and overlay it by position instead.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="aj-popup__controls">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="aj-popup__nav aj-popup__nav--prev"
          data-aj-prev
          aria-label="Previous shop"
        >&#8249;</button>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="aj-popup__nav aj-popup__nav--next"
          data-aj-next
          aria-label="Next shop"
        >&#8250;</button>
          <span class="aj-popup__count" data-aj-count aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Tabs, and they are real buttons: this is a picker, not a decoration.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul class="aj-popup__tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="{{ 'Choose a shop' }}">
        {%- for block in shops -%}
          <li role="presentation">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="aj-popup__tab"
              data-aj-tab
              role="tab"
              aria-selected="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
            >
              {{ block.settings.name }}
            </button>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>

      {%- comment -%}
        THE ACTUAL CONTENT, AND IT IS NEVER REMOVED.

        Once the book is running this list is hidden from EYES ONLY — clipped,
        not `display: none`. Display-none would take it out of the accessibility
        tree, and since the cards inside the book are aria-hidden and
        unfocusable, that would leave a screen-reader user with no route to any
        shop at all. This list is that route, and with no JavaScript it is also
        the visible one.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul class="aj-popup__plain">
        {%- for block in shops -%}
          <li>
            <a href="{{ block.settings.link | default: '#' }}">{{ block.settings.name }}</a>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Pop-up shops",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "aj-popup-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A pop-up book whose pop-up is a shop. Each block is one shop: give it a name, a link and its own artwork. NOTE: calling these pop-ups promises they are temporary — rotate them, or rename the section."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Heading", "default": "Pop-up shops" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subtitle",
      "label": "Sub-heading",
      "default": "Here for a while. Then something else."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "title_size",
      "label": "Heading size",
      "min": 24,
      "max": 72,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 40
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "auto",
      "label": "Turn pages on its own",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Off by default: turning the page is the point, and a book that turns itself argues with whoever is reading it. Stops for good the moment anyone touches it."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "interval",
      "label": "Seconds per shop, when turning on its own",
      "min": 3,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "s",
      "default": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background",
      "label": "Background",
      "default": "#ffffff"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "shop",
      "name": "Shop",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Shop name", "default": "Skate Shop" },
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Artwork",
          "info": "What pops up. Transparent PNG or SVG reads best against the paper."
        },
        { "type": "url", "id": "link", "label": "Link" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "blurb",
          "label": "Small line under the name",
          "default": "Open now"
        },
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "scenery",
          "label": "Backdrop cut-out",
          "info": "What this shop IS, in one wide silhouette — a vert ramp, a court, a green and a flagstick. Transparent PNG or SVG; it stands at the back of the set."
        },
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "scenery_mid",
          "label": "Middle cut-out",
          "info": "Optional second piece, standing between the backdrop and the logo."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 8,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Pop-up shops",
      "blocks": [{ "type": "shop" }, { "type": "shop" }, { "type": "shop" }]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
